From: ProAudio Player <noreply@proaudio-player.local>
Date: Tue, 15 Sep 2026 14:20:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] networkd: stabilize AP to station provisioning

The setup portal currently tears down dnsmasq and deactivates the setup
connection, then immediately asks NetworkManager to connect to the requested
SSID. On brcmfmac this races the AP-to-station transition: NetworkManager can
miss an otherwise valid SSID, while the failure path starts another scan on
top of a scan already pending in wpa_supplicant. The result is repeated
"No network with SSID" failures, rejected scan triggers and large bursts of
brcmfmac channel errors.

Fully stop and remove the setup AP before entering station mode, allow the
interface to settle, and request a directed scan for the selected SSID. Retry
the directed scan a few times without stacking broad scans. If the SSID still
does not appear in NetworkManager's cache, use its documented hidden=yes
first-connect path so mobile/hidden hotspots can respond to a directed probe.

Do not run the broad portal scan in the connection failure path. The existing
cached list is sufficient to render the portal, and a later connection attempt
will perform its own directed scan.

Upstream: not applicable (ProAudio Player local package)
Signed-off-by: Bohdan Cherniak <70845142+bodzey@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 proaudio-networkd | 58 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 54 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/proaudio-networkd b/proaudio-networkd
--- a/proaudio-networkd
+++ b/proaudio-networkd
@@ -1,18 +1,68 @@
+    def _wifi_cache_contains(self, ssid):
+        result = self.nmcli(
+            "-t", "-e", "yes", "-f", "SSID",
+            "device", "wifi", "list", "ifname", self.iface,
+            "--rescan", "no", timeout=10,
+        )
+        if result.returncode != 0:
+            return False
+        return any(
+            split_escaped(line)[0] == ssid
+            for line in result.stdout.splitlines()
+            if line
+        )
+
+    def _prepare_station_connection(self, ssid):
+        # A Broadcom SDIO interface needs a short settling window after leaving
+        # AP mode. Fully remove the setup profile first so NetworkManager cannot
+        # auto-reactivate it while the supplicant is switching back to STA mode.
+        self.stop_ap()
+        self.nmcli("radio", "wifi", "on", timeout=10)
+        self.configure_regdomain()
+        time.sleep(0.75)
+
+        # Refresh only the requested SSID instead of starting a broad scan while
+        # the previous AP->STA transition is still pending. NetworkManager's
+        # directed scan also makes first-time hidden/mobile hotspots discoverable.
+        for attempt in range(3):
+            result = self.nmcli(
+                "device", "wifi", "rescan", "ifname", self.iface,
+                "ssid", ssid, timeout=12,
+            )
+            if result.returncode == 0:
+                deadline = time.monotonic() + 4
+                while time.monotonic() < deadline:
+                    if self._wifi_cache_contains(ssid):
+                        return True
+                    time.sleep(0.4)
+            else:
+                message = result.stderr.strip() or result.stdout.strip()
+                LOG.info(
+                    "Directed Wi-Fi scan for %s attempt %d/3 deferred: %s",
+                    ssid, attempt + 1, message or "scan busy",
+                )
+            time.sleep(0.75 * (attempt + 1))
+        return self._wifi_cache_contains(ssid)
+
     def _connect_worker(self, ssid, password):
         time.sleep(1)
         try:
-            self.stop_dnsmasq()
-            self.nmcli("connection", "down", SETUP_PROFILE, timeout=10)
+            visible = self._prepare_station_connection(ssid)
             self._delete_connection(WIFI_PROFILE)
             args = [
-                "--wait", "25",
+                "--wait", "30",
                 "device", "wifi", "connect", ssid,
                 "ifname", self.iface,
                 "name", WIFI_PROFILE,
             ]
             if password:
                 args += ["password", password]
-            result = self.nmcli(*args, timeout=35)
+            if not visible:
+                # A phone hotspot may suppress beaconing until a directed probe
+                # arrives. NetworkManager documents hidden=yes for exactly this
+                # first-connection case.
+                args += ["hidden", "yes"]
+            result = self.nmcli(*args, timeout=40)
             if result.returncode == 0:
                 self.nmcli(
                     "connection", "modify", WIFI_PROFILE,
@@ -28,7 +78,9 @@
             LOG.warning("Wi-Fi provisioning failed for %s: %s", ssid, error)
             self._delete_connection(WIFI_PROFILE)
             self.set_error(f"Не вдалося підключитися до «{ssid}». Перевірте пароль і спробуйте ще раз.")
-            self.scan()
+            # Do not start another scan here. A failed `wifi connect` can leave
+            # a scan request pending; overlapping it with scan() is what caused
+            # repeated `Reject scan trigger` and brcmfmac channel-error storms.
             self.start_ap()
         except Exception as exc:
             LOG.exception("Помилка підключення до Wi-Fi")
